 {"id":"fabro-1dc9","title":"conductor: reached=blocked routes as 'Develop child failed' — revisor leg skipped for every slow-gate PR since deploy #6","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T16:44:03.054Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:10:15.437Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"REGRESSION since deploy #6 (2026-09-07 ~13:29 Berlin): conductor passes 01M1Y0ZE7K (15:30), 01M1Y2PF7V (16:00... UTC 13:30/14:00/15:34/16:00) ALL skip the revise leg. Evidence (16:00 UTC pass 01M1Y9J6J3DN server.log): develop child 01M1Y9N7R4 succeeded and PR #43 sat in a running gate; the develop-leg's second fabro_run_wait (until=merged) returned after 3s with reached=blocked (PR #34 semantics: open PR + non-green gate); the leg routed Edge 'develop -> exit' label='Develop child failed' -> soft park. The revise leg ONLY ran on passes whose PR was already merged at wait time (10:00/12:00/13:00 UTC passes, revisors 11:07/12:34/13:08). CONSEQUENCE: four develop runs unreviewed, no revisor seeds for them, and the line burns develop cycles without its feedback organ. FIX DIRECTIONS: (a) develop-leg routing must treat reached=blocked as 'merge pending', not failure: re-wait until=merged with a bounded deadline (e.g. 2-3 chained waits), and only route Failed on terminal-failed children (child status, not PR state); (b) after merged OR after child-terminal+parked-for-gate, ALWAYS run the revise leg; (c) backfill: the survey leg should detect completed develop runs without a revisor pass (no revisor journal/review artifact for the run id) and trigger a catch-up revise; (d) regression test: conductor graph routing on wait results terminal|merged|closed_unmerged|blocked|timeout maps blocked to wait-again/revise, never to the failed exit.","labels":["workflows","revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-07T18:10:15.437Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-5bee","title":"ci: bump Swatinem/rust-cache to v2.9.2 — Node 20 deprecation warning in the action gates","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T17:25:44.212Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T17:27:49.436Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Evidence: the warning was observed in the dogfood-gate run of PR #33 (2026-09-07 morning, user finding) — not in a current run; it fires on EVERY gate run as long as the old pin stands (GitHub changelog 2025-09-19: deprecation of Node 20 runners): 'Node.js 20 is deprecated. The following actions target Node.js 20 but are being forced to run on Node.js 24: Swatinem/rust-cache@779680da715d629ac1d338a641029a2f4372abb5'. The pinned SHA (comment '# v2') is an old v2 tag predating the node24 runtime. FIX: bump all 5 occurrences (.github/workflows/dogfood-gate.yml:62, .github/workflows/rust.yml:66,95,112,138) to Swatinem/rust-cache@6323deb102c322ba6fcbdcafc7e3dddab59af2b6 with comment '# v2.9.2' (v2.9.2 released 2026-08-06, commit SHA resolved via the annotated tag 63fed3e2 -> 6323deb1). Keep the repo's SHA-pinning style (no floating tags). Acceptance: grep shows the new SHA at all 5 sites; one gate run after the change shows no Node deprecation warning.","labels":["ci"]}
 {"id":"fabro-8275","title":"Downgrade the by-design preamble allow-key absence warn to info","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:17:29.202Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:21:27.438Z","description":"In the preamble fidelity module of fabro-workflow, the warn 'preamble_allow_keys entry absent … key=output.gate_known_bug_hits' fired on a green first-visit stage of develop run 01M1YGJ7JSWAVWJT45DRDZ89Z6, even though key absence on first visit is by design and fires on every clean run. Change: emit info (not warn) when an allow-listed context key is absent on a node's first visit; keep warn for repeat visits or genuine contract regressions. Expected effect: warn-level logs stop crying wolf on every green run while real fidelity regressions stay visible. Related but distinct from fabro-meta-c454 (input-contract closure, not log level).\nBasis: run 01M1YGJ7JSWAVWJT45DRDZ89Z6, workflow version 4ff76f32665f954e9a8e2027ec2a4a5b48266707730ae0620fcfd3f79acd4a10, commit f7126d9612d28110fca518d3aeeeb941bd7b659d","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-22e4","title":"agent: edit-tool file writes land with mtime 1970-01-01 — cargo skips recompiles, edits silently lag until manual touch","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.569Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:33:03.771Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"From unreviewed run 01M1Y2SMEVDHAFB59GZV9B84CQ (PR #41 implementer; recovered via journal sweep 2026-09-07 after the run aged out of revisor freshness): edit-tool file writes landed with mtime 1970-01-01 (e.g. lib/components/fabro-validate/src/file_refs.rs), so cargo considered the sources older than cached rlibs and silently skipped recompiles — a just-added pub fn was reported missing and behavior lagged the edits until a manual touch. This is silent cache poisoning of the build loop: any agent edit can produce a stale-binary diagnosis that costs implementer revisits. Fix direction: the platform's file-write path (edit tool / sandbox write transport) must set a real mtime — utimensat/write-with-times after creating or replacing the file so downstream build systems see fresh sources. Acceptance: an edit-tool write produces mtime == wall clock (unit test on the write path); a before/after cargo check in a scratch crate recompiles after an agent edit without manual touch.","labels":["engine","agent"]}
+{"id":"fabro-22e4","title":"agent: edit-tool file writes land with mtime 1970-01-01 — cargo skips recompiles, edits silently lag until manual touch","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.569Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:51:48.005Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"From unreviewed run 01M1Y2SMEVDHAFB59GZV9B84CQ (PR #41 implementer; recovered via journal sweep 2026-09-07 after the run aged out of revisor freshness): edit-tool file writes landed with mtime 1970-01-01 (e.g. lib/components/fabro-validate/src/file_refs.rs), so cargo considered the sources older than cached rlibs and silently skipped recompiles — a just-added pub fn was reported missing and behavior lagged the edits until a manual touch. This is silent cache poisoning of the build loop: any agent edit can produce a stale-binary diagnosis that costs implementer revisits. Fix direction: the platform's file-write path (edit tool / sandbox write transport) must set a real mtime — utimensat/write-with-times after creating or replacing the file so downstream build systems see fresh sources. Acceptance: an edit-tool write produces mtime == wall clock (unit test on the write path); a before/after cargo check in a scratch crate recompiles after an agent edit without manual touch.","labels":["engine","agent"],"closedAt":"2026-09-07T18:51:48.005Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-b8ed","title":"develop: verification-only briefs must not assert 'criteria satisfied' — derive per-criterion checks instead","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.670Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.670Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"From unreviewed run 01M1Y852BN91NSVSHFWNWTW5ST (PR #42; journal sweep 2026-09-07): the verification-only brief asserted 'acceptance criteria appear already satisfied', but criterion 5 of fabro-5e09 was materially unmet in the worktree — docs/agents/issue-tracker.md still said 'Filers assign at creation' and 'Assignment is a user decision', contradicting the seed's D2/D3 decisions from the same day. The pass only converged because the implementer re-checked; a lazier one would have closed the seed on the brief's word. Fix direction: the planner's verification-only brief generation must not carry satisfaction assertions — instead list each acceptance criterion with an instruction to verify it against the CURRENT worktree and report per-criterion status in the summary. Related: fabro-578a (different aspect: allowed command level in verification-only briefs).","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-52a9","title":"conductor survey: reword misleading 'burns the backlog down' claim — backlog journal is visibility-only, drain needs the revisor's newest-first rule to change","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.771Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.771Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"PR #45's survey prompt says 'the revisor revises the newest revisable run, so each subsequent pass burns the backlog down one run at a time' — but the revise leg creates the revisor without a goal and the revisor's select rule picks the NEWEST unrevised fresh run (which is always the current pass's own child), so the backlog NEVER drains; additionally the freshness rule (ADR-0015) makes older runs stale-evidence the moment the workflow version drifts, permanently disqualifying them. The journal line is dead-letter optimism (user + agent analysis 2026-09-07). Fix: reword survey.md to state the truth — the backlog entry is VISIBILITY-only (unreviewed run ids stay observable), runs are only revisable while fresh, and a real drain would need the revise leg to pass an explicit backlog run id in the goal (a decision not made). Do not promise behavior the graph cannot deliver.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
